      ],
      "image": "assets/images/62825/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C). Place pork tenderloins into a roasting pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/eeG_wF581ogPs8DDXyMzNa9K4Ao=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/62825-honey-glazed-pork-tenderloin-3x4-step2-3914-d7a234f991d24ff2a5a139a3f508d872.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/62825/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir honey, soy sauce, sesame oil, vinegar, and brown sugar together in a bowl until well blended.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Mt4fDufx0yuApYcGGiF6YA9u718=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/62825-honey-glazed-pork-tenderloin-3x4-step3-3917-a371b7daa2f34f198ad3783aa36958c5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/62825/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast tenderloins in the preheated oven for 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/--4ry5sfv0ZmYOVnXlL__CbRZx8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/62825-honey-glazed-pork-tenderloin-3x4-step4-3922-8623365ec8b143a1853c9084734aedf5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/62825/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce the temperature to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), and baste tenderloins with honey sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/wGu4zuXAAG-Z2jYDoz9jvRXgmg8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/62825-honey-glazed-pork-tenderloin-3x4-step4-3927-2f69cf0977c74f8fa425f110af2c3041.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/62825/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue to roast, basting a few more times with remaining sauce, until pork is slightly pink in the center, about 45 more minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
